=== SURVEY ===
Web source RouteAnnouncer.tsx is the SPA route-change screen-reader announcer. It mounts once near
the top of <App/>, subscribes to react-router `useLocation()`, and on every pathname change AFTER
the first render schedules a 100 ms `setTimeout` that reads `document.title` and writes it into a
single polite `<VisuallyHidden liveRegion priority="polite" data-testid="route-announcer">`
(role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"). Behaviour the test file pins:
  • first paint is SILENT (firstRender guard — the browser already speaks the landing title).
  • the read is DEFERRED (the new lazy page's usePageTitle must settle document.title first).
  • an EMPTY document.title CLEARS the region (setMessage('')), without speaking.
  • a rotating 0–3 zero-width-space suffix (`'\u200B'.repeat(announceCounter % 4)`) is appended so
    two consecutive routes that resolve to the SAME title both re-announce (e.g. /charging/1 ->
    /charging/2, both "Charging Session — TeslaSync").
  • effect cleanup CANCELS a pending read, so a rapid second navigation announces only the FINAL
    destination.
  • a `delayMs` prop overrides the 100 ms read delay.
Prompt-listed data sources (P1/S8): useLocation, useAnnouncer. Source truth: the component binds
`useLocation` and DELIBERATELY does NOT route through `useAnnouncer()` — its own doc comment
explains it owns a SEPARATE region so a noisy mutation announcement never clobbers a route change.
Reproduced faithfully: useLocation -> RouteAnnouncementCenter (the native router-location port);
the voicing uses a DEDICATED RouteAnnouncementPresenter (native parity of the component's own polite
region), NOT a shared announcer — matching the source's deliberate separation.
Shared components used by source: none. Charts/maps: none. i18n keys extracted: none (anonymous
surface — regions reproduced from source; all native chrome strings).
Existing native: no RouteAnnouncer/RouteAnnouncementCenter/RouteSnapshot/RouteAnnouncerModel/...
symbols (no collision). `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_).post()` already used in-repo
(Sources/App/AppShell.swift, sibling shared-surfaces/AnnouncerRegion.*) => the native voicing API is
valid here. AppRoute (Sources/App/AppRoute.swift) carries `path` + per-route `titleKey` — the native
useLocation pathname + page-title pairing the centre publishes.
Canonical surface pattern studied: sibling shared-surfaces/AnnouncerRegion (the 0001 a11y leaf:
Adapter/Model/Seams/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests/ModelTests) + CommandPalette.ViewTests
(view-composes-in-every-state pattern). Per-surface ownership is the codebase norm (235 surfaces
define their own *Telemetry, 132 their own *Connection enum, several their own ZWS-padding helper;
nothing outside AnnouncerRegion reuses its primitives) => RouteAnnouncer is fully self-contained.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component renders one sr-only region; the prompt requires a production-polished native
  surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and (native-chrome) i18n, every state visible
  (no blank box). Chosen: a native "route announcements inspector" — the polite live region presented
  visibly (the current announced page title + its role) over a recent-navigation log — while
  performing the REAL VoiceOver voicing (AccessibilityNotification, polite => .default queues, never
  interrupts) so the aria-live="polite" contract is reproduced, not merely drawn. Mirrors sibling
  AnnouncerRegion's native idiom.
- The web component's whole behaviour lives in a useEffect on [pathname, delayMs]; the native parity
  lives in the @Observable model, driven by a testable scheduler seam:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): RouteSnapshot (useLocation pathname + document.title), RouteAnnouncement
    (id = announceCounter, clean title + padded announcementText), RouteAnnouncerPadding (verbatim port
    of the `announceCounter % 4` zero-width-space dedupe), RouteAnnouncerLogic (the deferred read-time
    decision: empty title -> clear, else padded announcement), RouteAnnouncerAccessibility (VoiceOver
    label builders).
  • Model: RouteAnnouncerTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; RouteAnnouncementPresenter
    seam (native voicing boundary) + OSLog default; RouteAnnouncerConnection axis; RouteAnnouncerInput
    snapshot; RouteAnnouncerResolved + Projection (loading/empty/error/data); @Observable
    RouteAnnouncerModel — skips the first route, arms a DEFERRED read on each pathname change
    (cancelling any pending one), reads the freshest title at fire time, clears on empty, posts the
    rotating padded announcement once, one-shot stale auto-refresh.
  • Strings: RouteAnnouncerStrings i18n facade (P1/S10 table "RouteAnnouncer") — split out for the
    SwiftLint 400-line file budget.
  • Seams: RouteAnnouncerScheduler (TaskRouteAnnouncerScheduler = production setTimeout/clearTimeout
    port; ManualRouteAnnouncerScheduler = deterministic virtual clock = web vi.advanceTimersByTime),
    RouteAnnouncementCenter (the useLocation router-location port) + subscription, RouteAnnouncerSource
    protocol, Live + InMemory sources, AccessibilityRouteAnnouncementPresenter (real polite voicing).
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests/SeamsTests/ViewTests.
- States rendered (P4 leaf contract — no hidden surface): loading (skeleton region card), empty
  (nothing announced yet — the web region silent on first paint, a friendly TSEmptyState, never blank),
  error (retry — web QueryError peer), data (live region card + recent-navigation log), and the
  orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale
  transition).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/sr-only literally (native has no aria-live — used the platform
  AccessibilityNotification); a truly invisible surface (the P4 leaf contract forbids blank boxes —
  rendered the region visibly as an inspector); routing through a shared announcer (the source
  deliberately owns its own region — kept a dedicated presenter); direct posting / timers in the view
  (routed through the presenter + scheduler seams so the deferred-read behaviour is unit-testable);
  HTTP in the view (bound via the source seam); reusing sibling AnnouncerRegion primitives (codebase
  norm is per-surface ownership — duplicating the tiny ZWS helper here is the documented pattern, not
  the forbidden copy-paste).

